  "caption": "Quinn's favourite pose was the flamingo: one leg, all day, heavy bag on one shoulder. Then came a one-sided ache by the dimple above the bum.\n\nThe SI joints are strong and move only a few millimetres, so they don't slip out of place. Pain here is more about sensitivity and load, and one-sided habits can stir it up.\n\nWhat often helps: spread the load (stand on both feet, skip leg-crossing, swap bag sides), take stairs one at a time during flares, and build the glutes and hips with bridges, side-lying leg lifts and step-ups. Many people improve over 4–8 weeks.\n\nGet it checked if you have morning stiffness over 30 minutes, night pain, fever or symptoms that keep worsening.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
